# EENK Tests

This directory contains the automated tests for the EENK project. 

The tests run in a native PC environment (`native`) which mocks the hardware interfaces (like the E-Ink display, SD card, and preferences) using SDL2 and standard library features. This allows testing logic, rendering, and fonts without needing physical hardware.

## How to Run the Tests

To run the full test suite, you can use the PlatformIO CLI:

```bash
pio test -e native
```

When you run this command, PlatformIO will:
1. Compile the native test environment.
2. Run all tests inside `test_main.cpp`.
3. Output the success/failure status of each test case.

Visual screenshot tests generate actual `.bmp` files of the display output and compare them pixel-by-pixel against the golden reference images located in the `test/golden` directory. If a test fails, you can inspect the generated `.bmp` file to see the difference.
